WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.979
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:09.002
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:16.470
Unit twenty-seven: Education Policy. Today you will urge reform using it is high time + past.

4
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.446
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.598
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.055
Education policy.

7
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:32.010
Education policy means government decisions on how schools and learning are organised.

8
00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:36.532
Education policy shapes opportunities for a generation.

9
00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:40.582
Your turn. Say: Education policy.

10
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:45.282
Education policy.

11
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:47.053
Access.

12
00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:51.176
Access means the ability to reach or use a service.

13
00:00:51.783 --> 00:00:55.292
Access to schools remains uneven in rural areas.

14
00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:58.640
Your turn. Say: Access.

15
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.582
Access.

16
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:04.260
Quality.

17
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.399
Quality means the standard of how good something is.

18
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:11.947
Quality, not only enrolment, determines learning.

19
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.959
Your turn. Say: Quality.

20
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.662
Quality.

21
00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:20.348
Teachers.

22
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.418
Teachers means professionals who instruct students.

23
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.608
Teachers are the most important school resource.

24
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:31.124
Your turn. Say: Teachers.

25
00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:34.863
Teachers.

26
00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:36.711
Curriculum.

27
00:01:37.717 --> 00:01:40.482
Curriculum means the subjects and content taught.

28
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:43.733
The curriculum now includes digital skills.

29
00:01:44.317 --> 00:01:46.876
Your turn. Say: Curriculum.

30
00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:50.734
Curriculum.

31
00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:52.461
Equity.

32
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:57.017
Equity means fairness in the distribution of opportunities.

33
00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:00.766
Equity means extra support for those who start behind.

34
00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.107
Your turn. Say: Equity.

35
00:02:06.967 --> 00:02:07.875
Equity.

36
00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:09.618
Assessment.

37
00:02:10.617 --> 00:02:13.812
Assessment means the evaluation of what students have learned.

38
00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:17.809
Assessment should reward understanding, not memorisation.

39
00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:21.232
Your turn. Say: Assessment.

40
00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:25.219
Assessment.

41
00:02:25.983 --> 00:02:27.170
Outcomes.

42
00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:32.667
Outcomes means the results of an education, such as skills and employment.

43
00:02:33.283 --> 00:02:35.759
Learning outcomes improved after the reform.

44
00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:38.968
Your turn. Say: Outcomes.

45
00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:43.032
Outcomes.

46
00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:47.554
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:53.461
Visal, my teacher has a second job because her salary is so low. Is that normal?

48
00:02:54.550 --> 00:03:00.987
Sadly it is common. It is high time teachers were paid more, since quality depends on them.

49
00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:03.677
What else needs changing?

50
00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:14.945
It is high time assessment rewarded understanding, not memorisation, and it is high time rural schools were given equal resources.

51
00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.365
Why hasn't it happened?

52
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:27.314
Reform is costly and slow. But it is about time we treated education as an investment, not an expense.

53
00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.037
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:30.883 --> 00:03:33.951
Grammar focus: It is high time plus past.

55
00:03:34.251 --> 00:03:35.438
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.509
It is high time teachers were paid more.

57
00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:42.391
It is high time assessment rewarded understanding.

58
00:03:43.283 --> 00:03:46.664
It is about time rural schools were given equal resources.

59
00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:58.228
It is (high / about) time + subject + PAST simple expresses urgency about the present: It is high time teachers were paid more (not 'are paid'). The past tense signals that the action is overdue.

60
00:03:58.983 --> 00:04:03.180
Be careful! Don't say: It is high time teachers are paid more.

61
00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.853
Say: It is high time teachers were paid more.

62
00:04:08.153 --> 00:04:10.257
high time + past tense.

63
00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:13.603
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.877
Overdue Reforms.

65
00:04:16.177 --> 00:04:22.217
Education systems around the world have expanded access, but quality and equity often lag behind.

66
00:04:23.233 --> 00:04:30.585
Research consistently shows that teachers matter more than any other school resource, yet they are frequently underpaid and undertrained.

67
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.665
It is high time teachers were paid more and that assessment rewarded understanding, not memorisation.

68
00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:44.647
Rural and poorer schools also need equal resources, so that a child's birthplace no longer decides learning outcomes.

69
00:04:45.633 --> 00:04:51.592
Education policy must be treated as long-term investment rather than short-term expense.

70
00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.748
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:57.583 --> 00:05:00.059
It is high time teachers blank paid more.

72
00:05:00.359 --> 00:05:03.397
A, were. B, are. C, will be.

73
00:05:06.933 --> 00:05:08.886
The answer is A: were.

74
00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.827
The evaluation of what students have learned is blank.

75
00:05:13.127 --> 00:05:17.118
A, assessment. B, curriculum. C, access.

76
00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.852
The answer is A: assessment.

77
00:05:24.017 --> 00:05:27.015
Fairness in the distribution of opportunities is blank.

78
00:05:27.315 --> 00:05:30.980
A, quality. B, equity. C, outcomes.

79
00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:36.533
The answer is B: equity.

80
00:05:37.683 --> 00:05:39.509
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:39.809 --> 00:05:47.502
A, It is high time we changed the system.. B, It is high time we change the system.. C, It is high time we will change the system..

82
00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:54.390
The answer is A: It is high time we changed the system..

83
00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:59.279
According to the reading, teachers matter more than any other school…

84
00:05:59.579 --> 00:06:03.024
A, resource. B, rule. C, subject.

85
00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.822
The answer is A: resource.

86
00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:13.220
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:14.083 --> 00:06:17.441
What single change would most improve education where you live?

88
00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.808
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:36.108 --> 00:06:59.699
The single most useful change would be to raise teacher quality and pay. It is high time teachers were treated as professionals, with good training, fair salaries and time to plan lessons. Better teachers improve every other part of the system, from curriculum to assessment. Buildings and technology help, but they cannot replace a skilled teacher.

90
00:06:59.999 --> 00:07:01.801
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:02.717 --> 00:07:07.215
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and it is high time plus past.

92
00:07:07.515 --> 00:07:12.803
Today's value is educational equity. Every learner deserves a fair chance to succeed.

93
00:07:13.103 --> 00:07:15.918
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:07:16.218 --> 00:07:20.217
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

